build: 2026-06-23 v10.64.0 (FIX black immersive — header monitor no longer fights the GPU; + version centred + tuning cores)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notes: Founder device video (v10.62) analysed frame-by-frame: the full-screen immersive visual rendered BLACK for ~3 s at a stretch (14–16.5 s) then recovered. Root cause = GPU contention: the v10.62 header immersive monitor was a SECOND live MetalBioView (MTKView) running concurrently with the full-screen immersive (showVisual fullScreenCover, with WorkspaceView.topBar still rendering behind it) — two MTKViews starved each other. FIX: the header immersive monitor is now a LIGHTWEIGHT SwiftUI preview (radial bio-colour that pulses at the live heart rate, hue follows coherence) instead of a Metal view, so only ONE MetalBioView ever renders at a time; tapping still opens the real Metal immersive. Also lower GPU/battery. Audio of the clip was analysed (steady −10…−18 dBFS, no gaps/clipping) — the v10.61 stop-hang fix holds, no audio fault. This build also carries: header version moved small+centred under the brand (v10.63), and the verified TuningDetector + PitchTracker analysis cores (Kammerton + key from audio, unit-tested on CI) toward the "hear the tuning" feature. iOS compile gate + ci.yml validate.
